  "goodToKnow": "Die Sternwarte is an observatory. Many German towns have public Volkssternwarten run by amateur astronomy clubs. Berlin's Archenhold-Sternwarte, opened in 1896, houses the longest movable refracting telescope in the world, the Großer Refraktor, 21 metres long; Albert Einstein gave his first public Berlin lecture on relativity there in 1915. Die Warte means lookout. Plural: die Sternwarten."
